\item $D_f(0)=-\frac1{2\zeta(2)}=-\frac c2$.
\item $\Res_{s=-1/2}D_f(s)=\frac12\zeta(-\frac12)H_f(-\frac12)$, so that $K_f=-\frac83\zeta(-\frac12)H_f(-\frac12)$. Moreover $H_f(-\frac12)>0$ and $K_f>0$, and $K_f$ is given by the absolutely convergent product \eqref{eq:K-intro}.
